% ============================================================================
% NS-SDN master bibliography
% ============================================================================
%
% One entry per work, under one canonical key, for everything the project
% cites: the published papers, the documentation, the proposal, the journal
% manuscript, and the PDFs kept in references/papers/.  This file is the
% source of truth.  docs/source/references.bib is a verbatim subset of it
% under the same keys.  The bibliographies shipped with the FLAIRS and IEEE
% ORSS papers and with the ICSRI proposal are frozen as submitted and keep
% their own keys; references/README.md maps those keys onto these.
%
% Key convention: first author's surname, year, one-word slug, all ASCII,
% all lower case (sitzmann2020siren).  The year is the year of the version
% cited, which is the published version where one exists; the version on
% disk, when it differs, is named in the comment above the entry.
%
% Comment lines above an entry:
%   PDF:       the file in references/papers/ that holds the work, if any,
%              and which version of the work that file is.
%   Cited by:  FLAIRS, ORSS, ICSRI, docs, journal, src (module docstrings).
%
% Encoding: plain ASCII with TeX accents ({\"u}, {\'e}) so the file works
% under both BibTeX and biber.
%
% ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
